WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
What does your wife do, if
you don't mind me asking?

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.433
Not at all.

00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:04.266
She's a Jesuit priest.

00:00:04.266 --> 00:00:05.821
Oh, okay.

00:00:05.821 --> 00:00:07.029
(laughing)

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:09.450
All right, come on, Jesuit.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.370
My wife, when I met
her, was in advertising.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.000
She was an advertising executive,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.470
and then when she got
pregnant with our first child,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.790
I think, she started, I
think was around then,

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.790
she started working on, her
real passion is writing.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.120
So she's been writing plays.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.160
She works with different
playwriting organizations

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.550
and theater groups,
and she's a dramaturge,

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.730
which means she reads other
people's plays and tries

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.330
to help them and gets, gets involved a lot

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.460
in independent theater,
and she works really hard,

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.293
very proud of her.

00:00:42.293 --> 00:00:44.383
She's a really smart.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.960
It's hilarious to see that,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.980
my bed stand and her bed stand.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.350
Hers, you know, mine is always like,

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.000
some cheesy historical murder mystery,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.510
and then her, hers is just like the great,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:02.300
you know, Aristotle and Plato and all the,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.300
just the, you know, Beckett,
all the great playwrights,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.290
and she's constantly
reading that stuff and I get

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.840
really intimidated because
she's, she's really brilliant.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.070
She's really smart and creative.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.330
Oh, I really like listening to people talk

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:21.880
about their significant
others because you can't

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.100
really see it, but I could see it.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.520
Your like, face changed
when you talked about her

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.330
and that's like, so magical.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:30.890
It's truly a dream,
and that's what I want.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.300
I want my face to change when I talk

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.850
about somebody that I love.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.037
I want their face to
change when someone's like,

00:01:37.037 --> 00:01:37.910
"Oh, who are you dating?"

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:38.899
And it's like,

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:40.920
"Oh, Nicole, she's so wonderful."

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.720
That, it's so magical.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.930
It was really lovely to see.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.930
Well, you know, I would
tell you, I, this can sound

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:55.150
very West Coast and
granola-y and spiritual

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.180
and I'm, I'm so not that
person but what I have come

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.830
to believe and I actually,
I talk to a lot of the women

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:01.920
in my office about this.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.760
I, I tell them like, my
big thing, when I talk

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.350
to younger women that work on the staff,

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.080
if they ever, you know,
holiday party or whatever,

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.910
and they're talking
about dating and how hard

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.560
it is right now, I just, my
big thing is don't settle.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.400
Like, do not settle.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.233
Don't settle.

00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:18.640
I did not settle, and
there's not a day in my life

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.690
when I don't think, oh
man, I, I've made good.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:26.270
I've had good ideas and
bad ideas, but 19 years ago

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.810
I made the exact right
call, and that's the way

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:32.430
you want to feel, and that's what you,

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.320
you just keep going 'til
you find that person.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.400
Like, that's, that's what you deserve.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.120
You deserve that, and,
and you do, you really do.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.700
Thank you, Conan.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.630
I think I deserve it too.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.560
You do.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.560
So, so I think that's why,
and I think what's gonna,

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:54.430
what helps you so much is you
really do know what you want

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.060
and you're a very confident,
attractive person.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.550
So that's just going to happen.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.660
It's just a question of when.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.506
It's going to happen when
you're not thinking about it.

00:03:02.506 --> 00:03:03.840
You know, you're going to be at a CVS

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.004
and you're going to bump into somebody.

00:03:05.004 --> 00:03:05.920
That's when it's, that's when it happens.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.400
That's what people say.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.410
They say, when you're
not thinking about it,

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.350
you're not looking for
it, that's when it happens

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.384
but I'm always thinking
about it and looking for it.

00:03:15.384 --> 00:03:17.634
(laughing)

